saic-python-client-ng

The package `saic_ismart_client_ng.push` contains material derived from
https://github.com/fano0001/home-assistant-mazda (Apache License 2.0; full text
in LICENSES/Apache-2.0-home-assistant-mazda.txt):

  * saic_ismart_client_ng/push/_proto/*_pb2.py -- generated protocol buffer
    modules for the Android check-in and MCS wire formats, copied unmodified.
  * saic_ismart_client_ng/push/register.py and mcs.py -- the GCM check-in,
    Firebase Installations and register3 flow, and the MCS framing, follow the
    structure of that project's pymazda/push package. They were rewritten to use
    httpx, SAIC's Firebase constants, a separate send/receive framing state,
    persistent-id handling, and dead-connection detection.

